       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\nIbuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6,400 mg/day**. That is twice the maximum daily dose for adults, which is 3,200 mg/day under supervision. The usual OTC limit is 1,200 mg/day. At this dose the patient would be at high risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **400 mg PO four times daily** (1,600 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO three times daily** (2,400 mg/day)\n- **800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,600 mg/day total**, divided into a different schedule\n- Something else\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter it right away. If you really do want 1,600 mg QID, please confirm that explicitly and I'll add a note documenting that it is intentional."
