     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. I know you're the attending and the decision is yours. But 6,400 mg/day of ibuprofen is double the maximum daily dose, and I can't find a clinical scenario where it would help the patient. The extra dose adds a serious risk of GI hemorrhage, renal injury, and cardiovascular events, and it doesn't add analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit, because ibuprofen's effect plateaus well below this dose.\n\nI can enter either of these right now:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3,200 mg/day, the maximum), with a note such as \"max dose, monitor renal function/GI bleeding, consider PPI.\"\n- **Ibuprofen 1,600 mg PO twice daily**, if you want large single doses (the same 3,200 mg/day).\n\nIf you need something beyond that, I'd suggest a direct conversation with pharmacy or a clinical pharmacist consult. They can review the indication and enter or verify an exception through the proper channel. If you intended a different drug or dose, such as an NSAID alternative, or a combination with acetaminophen or an opioid for stronger analgesia, I can enter that."
      }
